## Before every continuation of work

Read all three:

1. `docs/master_roadmap.md`
2. `docs/agent_coordination/CURRENT_TASK.md`
3. `docs/content_platform/ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md`

Also use `docs/content_platform/CONTENT_PLATFORM_SPEC.md` for architecture decisions.

Do not invent a second roadmap. Update the existing `docs/master_roadmap.md` only.

## Checklist discipline

* Every owner requirement is an atomic checkbox in `ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md`.
* Do **not** skip checkboxes.
* Do **not** merge many requirements into a vague “готово”.
* Mark `[x]` only when that item has **code + tests + Codex APPROVE** (docs-only items: Codex APPROVE on the docs package).
* If blocked, record the blocker in `CURRENT_TASK.md` and move to the next independent substage.

## Codex gates

* Before a stage/substage: send architecture + real schema findings to Codex.
* After implementation: send full diff + test results to Codex.
* Fix P0/P1 before APPROVE.
* No Stage/substage DONE without Codex APPROVE.
* After APPROVE: update checklist + CURRENT_TASK, then continue.

## Hard bans until owner says otherwise

* No remote Supabase migration apply
* No Edge Function deploy
* No GitHub push (including force-push)
* No real data import
* No `service_role` in Flutter Web / Admin Web
* No deleting existing production data
* No editing already-applied migrations
* Prefer extending existing tables; create new ones only with documented proof that extension is unsafe

## Stage 13 protection

Do not rewrite completed Stage 13 chats, group actions, news archive, or RBAC without confirmed necessity.
